### Orvexa API v1 — journey step 15: identity (OIDC, [O-29])
### Public login surface — mounted ONLY when the identity plane is configured
### (ORVEXA_OIDC_ISSUER / _CLIENT_ID / _CLIENT_SECRET all set). Without it the
### routes are not mounted: authorize-url answers the router's plain-text 404
### (not the JSON error envelope) — the API-key path is unchanged.
### Full contract: docs/rbac.md.

@ORVEXA_URL = {{$processEnv ORVEXA_URL}}

### Authorize-url bootstrap → 200 {authorize_url, state, nonce, expires_in,
### redirect_uri} (500 identity.discovery_failed when the IdP is unreachable)
# @name identityAuthorizeUrl
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/identity/authorize-url

###

### Callback: state validation → code exchange → ID-token verification →
### tenant-scoped principal info. Drive through the real IdP redirect
### (401 when state/exchange/verification fails, 404 when disabled).
# @name identityCallback
GET {{ORVEXA_URL}}/api/v1/identity/callback?code=probe&state=probe
